  "style": {
    "id": "multiplane-cel",
    "name": "Multiplane Cel",
    "description": "Classic hand-painted cel animation shot on a multiplane camera: a storybook landscape painted in flat gouache with visible brush strokes (sky, far hills, a meadow with a path and a cottage, a tree grove, dark foreground foliage) and one inked-and-painted cel bird animated on twos, each layer on its own sheet of glass. Inside the picture the camera pushes down through the stack and the layers part with strong parallax; pulled back, the truth: a vertical steel rig of six glass panes with lamps between the shelves, peg bars on every tray and a film camera looking straight down from the top. Sliding one pane sideways changes the picture (a grove slides off and reveals the cottage). Flat unlit paint, crisp black ink and flat colour on the cel with a soft cel shadow, faint glass sheen and a few dust specks.",
